# BROODMOTHER — a slim, pale woman grown out of the front of a fleshy spider
# body, in the lineage of Quake 1's Vore (Shalrath) but MEAT where the Vore is
# chitin. She is the roster's body-horror piece about desire: the upper half
# is built to be looked at — hourglass, three swollen mammary orbs, full
# glossy lips, a fine nose, glowing eyes — and the lower half is what the eye
# arrives at after it has been caught. The design problem is that tension:
# every beat below is ATTRACTIVE AT THE TOP AND WRONG BY THE TIME YOU LOOK
# TWICE. Neither half is allowed to win.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE (owner brief, 2026-09-22: "female enemy monster ... big
# mammary orb glands but like three of them. her face is grotesque but
# somewhat beautiful, big lips but slim nose and glowing eyes. she is slim but
# the bottom half her body is like a spider ... like the vore from quake 1 but
# more fleshy"). There is no mesh and no plate, so blob:measure / blob:rings
# exit 2 and NO number below is measured — every one is a design decision with
# its reason beside it, as ogre.blob and gnasher.blob do.
#
# THE BEATS that carry the silhouette:
#   1. THE HOURGLASS ON EIGHT LEGS. A wasp waist (0.19 m across) between a
#      narrow ribcage and flared hips, and the hips do not end in legs — they
#      melt into a cephalothorax. From the front at distance she reads as a
#      woman standing in a thicket of bent sticks; the spider arrives second.
#   2. THREE ORBS. Two high, one lower in the middle, set in a triangle so
#      that from the front the count is legible (a row of three does not fit
#      a slim ribcage without merging into one bolster). Taut, glossy, faintly
#      flushed paint — overstretched skin, not a soft body — each with a small
#      glowing gland pore in the same colour as the eyes, so the eye is pulled
#      between face and chest, which is the point.
#   3. THE FACE. Beautiful in its parts, wrong in its sum: a fine chamfered
#      nose and high sharp cheekbones on a narrow jaw, then lips too wide and
#      too full for that face, slanted glowing eyes, four small spider eyes
#      beaded across the forehead, and a long cranium swept back into a
#      crest — since the hair pass, a platinum ponytail of hairlock strands.
#      Every face feature is geometry (face.ts: painted faces read as a visor
#      or a zombie); the face block is a nub.
#   4. THE LEGS ARE FLESH. Spider geometry — femur up and out, knee high above
#      the body, tibia down to a pointed tarsus — but skin-coloured, with swollen
#      knuckle joints and only the last few cm of each foot hardened to a dark
#      nail. That is the "more fleshy than the Vore" beat.
#
# RIG LIMIT, said plainly: the motion layer (gait.ts jointNamesForBody) knows
# a humanoid's hip/knee/foot joints only. The spider leg bones map to no gait
# joint, so this pass is a STATIC body in the lab — she will render, turn and
# take wounds, but a walk needs a spider gait. That is the next piece of work,
# not something to fake by naming the front pair thigh/shin/foot.
model broodmother
  # Crown of the cranium (the crest sweeps back, not up). A slim 0.97 m of
  # woman rising from a spider body whose back rides at ~1.0 m, so she looks
  # DOWN at the player without being a brute — height here is reach and
  # elegance, not mass.
  height 1.97
  # No `stance`: the check classifies thigh/shin/foot knee folds, and she has
  # none. Omitted means "not checked", which is the truth (SKILL.md).

skeleton
  # The root is the JUNCTION where the woman leaves the spider: 0.90 -> 1.00.
  # Her waist starts at 1.00 — the height a standing woman's navel is at, so
  # the spider body replaces her from the hips down rather than being tacked
  # under her feet.
  root pelvis at 0.90 len=0.10

  # Her spine: nearly upright with a slight sway (lumbar forward 3, thoracic
  # back 4) — posture, not a hunch; the ogre is the hunched one.
  # Long on purpose (0.32 + 0.27): at 0.28 + 0.24 the knees rose to her
  # mid-chest and, from 3 m, she read as a small figure hemmed in by the
  # leg crowns. Now the whole bust clears them and she stands UP out of the
  # spider.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=3  len=0.32
  bone chest parent=spine  dir=up pitch=-4 len=0.27
  # A long neck carried forward 12 degrees and the head tipped back 4 — the
  # chin leads, which is a haughty carriage, and it clears the face off the
  # top orbs in profile.
  bone neck  parent=chest  dir=up pitch=12 len=0.11
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=-4 len=0.22

  # The spider abdomen: a bone leaving the junction BACKWARD and slightly up
  # (dir up pitch -80 = 80 degrees back from vertical), so the egg-sac mass
  # rides behind her at hip height and its crest does not rise over her back.
  bone abdomen parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-80 len=0.62

  mirror
    # Slim shoulders: 0.14 m of clavicle, tilted up 6 — a narrow woman's
    # shoulder line. The arms are LONG (0.33 + 0.30 + hand) and thin, hanging
    # a little forward and out so they clear the front legs' femurs.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    dir=side tilt=6 len=0.14
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=6  tilt=20 len=0.33
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down pitch=24 tilt=4  len=0.30
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=12         len=0.09

    # FOUR LEGS A SIDE. Every angle below was solved (scratch legs.mjs,
    # inverting blob-compile dirVector) from a leg laid out by YAW around the
    # cephalothorax centre (0, 0.90, -0.08): leg1 at 30 degrees off the nose,
    # leg2 68, leg3 108, leg4 145. That fan — front pair reaching forward past
    # her, back pair raking behind the abdomen — is what reads as SPIDER from
    # every yaw; four parallel legs read as a centipede.
    #
    # hubN is an INVISIBLE locator (no prims): the grammar attaches children
    # at the parent's tail and `side=` only offsets x, so a bone is the only
    # way to put a socket FORWARD or BACK of the junction. Each hub lands on
    # a socket 0.16-0.17 m out from the cephalothorax centre at y 0.92.
    #
    # Each leg: femur rises 42-48 degrees out to a knee at y 1.27-1.35 (level
    # with her lower ribs — the knees framing her is half the silhouette),
    # tibia drops 58-64 degrees, tarsus 78-80 degrees to a point on the floor.
    # Tarsus lengths were set so each tip lands at y ~0.
    bone hub1    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=27.4  tilt=45.0 len=0.127
    bone femur1  parent=hub1   dir=up   pitch=35.4  tilt=24.2 len=0.58
    bone tibia1  parent=femur1 dir=down pitch=27.3  tilt=17.4 len=0.88
    bone tarsus1 parent=tibia1 dir=down pitch=10.4  tilt=6.1  len=0.61

    bone hub2    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=-5.3  tilt=63.1 len=0.178
    bone femur2  parent=hub2   dir=up   pitch=15.6  tilt=43.8 len=0.54
    bone tibia2  parent=femur2 dir=down pitch=10.1  tilt=26.2 len=0.80
    bone tarsus2 parent=tibia2 dir=down pitch=3.7   tilt=9.3  len=0.60

    bone hub3    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=-36.3 tilt=63.7 len=0.224
    bone femur3  parent=hub3   dir=up   pitch=-13.3 tilt=46.6 len=0.52
    bone tibia3  parent=femur3 dir=down pitch=-7.8  tilt=24.9 len=0.78
    bone tarsus3 parent=tibia3 dir=down pitch=-3.1  tilt=9.5  len=0.58

    bone hub4    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=-60.0 tilt=48.9 len=0.244
    bone femur4  parent=hub4   dir=up   pitch=-34.7 tilt=29.0 len=0.56
    bone tibia4  parent=femur4 dir=down pitch=-24.2 tilt=18.3 len=0.86
    bone tarsus4 parent=tibia4 dir=down pitch=-9.8  tilt=7.0  len=0.58
  end

body
  # ---- THE SPIDER BODY (torso cluster) --------------------------------------
  # Cephalothorax: the fleshy hub every leg socket sits on. Centre
  # (0, 0.90, -0.08) — the point the leg yaws were laid out around. Longer
  # than wide (deep 1.35), and low (tall 0.75) so it reads as a body slung
  # between the knees rather than a ball.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 r=0.200 wide=1.15 tall=0.75 deep=1.35 blend=0.050 offset=(0,0,-0.080)
  # Her HIPS: flared wider than the ribcage (semi-width 0.16 vs 0.13) — the
  # bottom of the hourglass — and blended wide into the cephalothorax so the
  # woman grows out of the spider rather than sitting on it.
  blob torso on pelvis at=1.00 r=0.120 wide=1.35 tall=0.80 deep=1.00 blend=0.060 offset=(0,0.020,0.015)

  # THE ABDOMEN — an egg sac, not a chitin bulb. Big (semi 0.32 x 0.28 x
  # 0.41), riding BEHIND her at hip height (the bone runs 80 degrees back),
  # dropped 6 cm so its crest stays below her shoulder blades in profile.
  blob torso on abdomen at=0.72 r=0.300 wide=1.05 tall=0.92 deep=1.35 blend=0.070 offset=(0,-0.060,0)
  # Pedicel: the narrow waist between cephalothorax and abdomen, a spider's
  # tell. Slightly UNDER-width so the two masses read as two.
  bar  torso on abdomen from=0.05 to=0.40 r=0.110 wide=0.95 tall=0.85 blend=0.040 offset=(0,-0.050,0)
  # Swellings on the sac: three pustule blobs pushing out of the upper flank
  # and back. Painted a darker, wetter bruised rose so they read as something
  # growing INSIDE pressing out, not as skin folds. A saturated 8a3a44 read
  # as flat red STICKERS in the first close-up; this is her skin, congested.
  blob torso on abdomen at=0.65 r=0.090 blend=0.045 offset=(0.170,0.130,0.020) color=8e5d6c gloss=0.60
  blob torso on abdomen at=0.85 r=0.075 blend=0.040 offset=(-0.150,0.170,-0.010) color=8e5d6c gloss=0.60
  blob torso on abdomen at=1.00 r=0.065 blend=0.036 offset=(0.060,0.120,-0.120) color=8e5d6c gloss=0.60
  # Spinneret: a short tapered teat at the rear underside, pointing back and
  # down. r2 tapers it; the tip is left blunt (r2 0.012), it is flesh.
  blob torso on abdomen at=1.00 r=0.050 r2=0.012 blend=0.020 chamfer offset=(0,-0.170,-0.200) tip=(0,-0.050,-0.080)

  # ---- HER TORSO -------------------------------------------------------------
  # Wasp waist: semi-width 0.095 — narrower than the hips (0.16) and the
  # ribcage (0.13). This is the hourglass; widen it and she becomes a torso.
  bar  torso on spine from=0.00 to=0.55 r=0.078 r2=0.085 wide=1.22 deep=0.85 blend=0.030
  # Ribcage: narrow, a little deeper at the back so the orbs sit ON it.
  blob torso on spine at=0.90 r=0.100 wide=1.28 tall=1.10 deep=0.86 blend=0.035
  # Upper chest — the structural mass the arms and neck fuse to. `core`
  # because the abdomen is the torso's fattest prim and clusterCore would
  # otherwise route every fuse probe through the egg sac.
  blob torso on chest at=0.50 r=0.100 wide=1.30 tall=1.00 deep=0.84 blend=0.035 core
  # Shoulder line: flat and narrow (semi 0.135). A woman's shoulders, not a
  # yoke.
  blob torso on chest at=0.95 r=0.070 wide=1.95 tall=0.55 deep=0.85 blend=0.030

  # THE THREE ORBS. Chest bone runs y 1.32 -> 1.59; at=0.42 puts the top pair
  # at y ~1.42. The ribcage's front is at z ~0.09, so a centre at z 0.075
  # with r 0.085 stands each orb 7 cm proud of the chest — big, in a slim
  # frame. The top pair sits at x +-0.095: 0.19 apart against a 0.17
  # diameter, so they do NOT merge; the third hangs 8.5 cm lower in the
  # middle and a touch further forward, nestled between and under them — the
  # triangle that keeps the count legible from the front. Painted a taut
  # flushed rose, glossy: overstretched skin. d9a3a0 was tried first and
  # read ORANGE against the cool skin — a costume, not her body; c99aa6
  # keeps her skin's cool cast and only flushes it. Small blend (0.016) so
  # they root into the chest without their outlines smearing into one mass.
  blob torso on chest at=0.42 r=0.085 blend=0.016 offset=(0.095,-0.010,0.075) both color=c99aa6 gloss=0.55
  blob torso on chest at=0.42 r=0.082 blend=0.016 offset=(0,-0.095,0.085) color=c99aa6 gloss=0.55
  # Gland pores — one per orb, on its forward pole, glowing in the EYES'
  # colour. Small (r 0.009) and half-buried so they read as a lit pore in
  # the skin, and so face and chest answer each other across the dark.
  blob torso on chest at=0.42 r=0.009 blend=0.003 offset=(0.100,-0.014,0.158) both color=ff2ea6 glow=0.55
  blob torso on chest at=0.42 r=0.009 blend=0.003 offset=(0,-0.100,0.165) color=ff2ea6 glow=0.55

  # ---- HEAD --------------------------------------------------------------
  # A long slim neck (r 0.040) — elegance is length. 0.036 read as a stalk.
  bar  head on neck from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.040 deep=1.05 blend=0.014
  # CRANIUM. Skull runs y 1.70 -> 1.92. Narrow (semi-width 0.075) and tall:
  # a fine head on a slim neck. The fattest head prim, so it is the frame any
  # future sheet would project from.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 r=0.092 wide=0.82 tall=1.12 deep=1.08 blend=0.010
  # THE CREST: the cranium continues back and UP into a long bald sweep (tip
  # 17 cm behind, 9 cm up) — the Giger read, and the first thing wrong about
  # her in silhouette. r2 narrows it so it ends in a rounded ridge, not a
  # second skull.
  # r2 0.030 / tip 17 cm read as a pointed HAT in the first frames; a fatter
  # end and a shorter, flatter sweep reads as the skull itself going on.
  # PAINTED AS HAIR since the hair pass: the crest is now a sleek, pulled-
  # back mass (a high ponytail's root), and the ponytail strands below hang
  # off its tip. The silhouette is unchanged; only its reading moved from
  # skull to hair.
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.080 r2=0.050 wide=0.80 blend=0.024 offset=(0,0.000,-0.030) tip=(0,0.060,-0.140) color=ddd6cc gloss=0.45

  # ---- HAIR (hairlock strands, owner ask 2026-09-22) ------------------------
  # Platinum (ddd6cc — c9b99a rendered GOLD after the sRGB lift and the warm
  # key): the bimbo archetype's colour, laid over the grotesque — and it
  # reads against both the pale skin and the dark room. The `strand=` prim is
  # schoolgirl-described's road (a mass for any VOLUME, strands for every
  # hanging EDGE) and strand-fixture.blob is its render gate.
  #
  # Scalp cap: a tight crown mass, pulled BACK (z -0.030) so its front edge
  # (z ~0.065) sits behind the spider eyes (z 0.078-0.090 at y ~1.86) — the
  # hairline rides above and behind them, and her forehead stays bare.
  blob head on skull at=0.58 r=0.088 wide=0.88 tall=0.92 deep=1.06 blend=0.006 offset=(0,0.018,-0.030) color=ddd6cc gloss=0.45
  # PONYTAIL: from the crest tip (0, ~1.89, -0.17) down 0.45 m to between
  # the shoulder blades, bowed back so it clears her spine (back of the
  # ribcage is at z ~-0.09; the tail rides -0.17..-0.25) and ends above the
  # abdomen's crest (y ~1.33). Tapered 0.040 -> 0.016 so it thins to points.
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.040 r2=0.016 wide=0.90 blend=0.004 offset=(0,0.055,-0.165) tip=(0,-0.450,-0.060) bend=(0,0.000,-0.050) strand=10 wave=0.14 cycles=3 fat=0.78 color=ddd6cc gloss=0.45
  # FACE-FRAMING LOCKS: temple to collarbone, in front of the ears and behind
  # the cheekbones' front (cheek z 0.068 vs lock z 0.01-0.05), bent out over
  # the curve of the jaw. They stop at y ~1.54, on the shoulder line, above
  # the top orbs (their tops ~1.50) — framing the face without covering the
  # chest.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 r=0.022 r2=0.010 blend=0.004 offset=(0.068,0.010,0.010) tip=(0.030,-0.260,0.040) bend=(0.020,0,0.030) strand=6 wave=0.18 cycles=3 fat=0.75 both color=ddd6cc gloss=0.45
  # Narrow jaw, set forward: a slim V-shaped lower face.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 r=0.062 wide=1.05 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.012 offset=(0,-0.010,0.035)
  # Pointed chin: a short chamfered taper forward-down off the jaw.
  blob head on skull at=0.08 r=0.026 r2=0.010 blend=0.008 chamfer offset=(0,-0.004,0.066) tip=(0,-0.018,0.022)
  # High, sharp cheekbones, set wide and forward: the "somewhat beautiful"
  # half. Chamfered so they keep an edge under the eyes. wide 1.10 at x 0.044:
  # at 1.35 / 0.048 they stood out past the cranium as a ledge and the head
  # read as a mushroom cap from the front.
  blob head on skull at=0.47 r=0.028 wide=1.10 tall=0.70 deep=0.90 blend=0.008 chamfer offset=(0.044,-0.012,0.068) both
  # SLIM NOSE: a fine chamfered ridge running from between the eyes down and
  # out, tapering r 0.009 -> 0.006. Its tip clears the face by ~1.5 cm
  # (cranium semi-depth ~0.099; tip at z 0.113) — enough to catch the light,
  # not enough to be a feature of its own. This is the refinement the lips
  # are measured against.
  blob head on skull at=0.52 r=0.009 r2=0.006 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0,0.010,0.093) tip=(0,-0.045,0.020)
  # LIPS — too big for this face, on purpose (6.4 cm across on a 15 cm-wide
  # head; the first 7 cm at r 0.013/0.017 filled the whole lower face and
  # read as a clown's mouth rather than a beautiful one gone too far). Each one BENT bar corner to corner, bowed forward over the jaw's
  # curve (the ogre's lips are the precedent). The lower one is fuller.
  # Corners at z 0.092 against a jaw surface of ~0.087 there, middles ~1 cm
  # proud. Dark wet plum, glossy — the one lush thing on a pale face.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 r=0.011 tall=0.90 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.032,0.004,0.094) tip=(0.064,0,0) bend=(0,0.008,0.030) color=7a2444 gloss=0.75
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 r=0.015 tall=0.85 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.029,-0.019,0.092) tip=(0.058,0,0) bend=(0,-0.008,0.032) color=7a2444 gloss=0.75
  # EYES — slanted almonds, GLOWING hot magenta. Each is a short capsule from
  # its inner corner out and UP (tip), half-buried in the cranium's front
  # (surface z ~0.088 at x 0.034), so the lid line is the cranium's own
  # surface. Magenta, not the ogre's red: seductive and unnatural at once.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.011 blend=0.003 offset=(0.024,0,0.086) tip=(0.022,0.007,-0.006) both color=ff2ea6 glow=0.95
  # SPIDER EYES — four small beads across the forehead above the real eyes,
  # the inner pair higher: a spider's secondary row. Dimmer (glow 0.7) so the
  # main eyes still lead.
  blob head on skull at=0.72 r=0.007 blend=0.002 offset=(0.017,0.012,0.090) both color=ff2ea6 glow=0.70
  blob head on skull at=0.70 r=0.006 blend=0.002 offset=(0.042,0.004,0.078) both color=ff2ea6 glow=0.70

  # ---- ARMS ----------------------------------------------------------------
  # Slim and long. Shoulder ball is the structural mass (core).
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.04 r=0.046 blend=0.016 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.08 to=0.96 r=0.038 r2=0.031 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.02 to=0.95 r=0.031 r2=0.022 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Narrow hand.
  blob arm on hand at=0.40 r=0.028 wide=0.80 tall=1.25 deep=1.15 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Three LONG fingers — 13 cm, a hand and a half — curving forward to dark
  # nails. tip sends each down and forward, splayed; r2=0 is a true point.
  # The spider in her hands.
  blob arm on hand at=0.85 r=0.010 r2=0.002 blend=0.004 offset=(0.012,0,0.010)  tip=(0.018,-0.110,0.060) bend=(0.004,0,0.020) mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60
  blob arm on hand at=0.85 r=0.010 r2=0.002 blend=0.004 offset=(0,0,0.016)      tip=(0,-0.125,0.065)     bend=(0,0,0.022)     mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60
  blob arm on hand at=0.85 r=0.010 r2=0.002 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.012,0,0.010) tip=(-0.016,-0.110,0.058) bend=(-0.004,0,0.020) mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60

  # ---- SPIDER LEGS (leg clusters: four legs a side) -------------------------
  # FOUR prims a leg, and that count is budgeted: the shader ceiling is 128
  # flesh + bone prims (validate.ts), and a first pass with separate coxa and
  # knuckle balls (7 a leg) came to 174. So each joint's swelling is built
  # into the taper instead: the femur starts fat (the coxa) and thins, the
  # tibia starts FATTER than the femur ends (0.040 vs 0.034) and so reads as a
  # knuckle of meat at the knee, and the same again at the ankle. Flesh
  # everywhere except the last 28% of each foot, a dark glossy nail — the
  # "more fleshy than the Vore" beat. Thick on purpose: at femur r 0.050 the
  # first frames read as a daddy-longlegs of bent sticks; at 0.066 they read
  # as meat, and the spread still dwarfs her so the spider is the first read.
  # The nail's r 0.013 is under half the tarsus's 0.030 on purpose: deriveBones
  # (MASS_FRACTION 0.5) then grows no bone in it, which is what keeps the
  # budget.
  # ONE coxa ball, on leg2, marked `core`: the fuse probe runs from the
  # cluster core's centre to the torso's, and from a femur's midpoint (out in
  # the air beside the knee) it crossed daylight and reported the legs
  # disconnected. A ball seated IN the cephalothorax at the socket gives the
  # probe a start inside flesh. The other three legs root by their fat femur
  # starts alone (fusedOf per leg is pinned in the test).
  bar  leg on femur1  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.066 r2=0.044 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  leg on tibia1  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.052 r2=0.027 blend=0.014 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus1 from=0.00 to=0.72 r=0.030 r2=0.013 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus1 from=0.72 to=1.00 r=0.013 r2=0.000 blend=0.003 chamfer mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60

  blob leg on femur2  at=0.00 r=0.068 blend=0.018 mirror core
  bar  leg on femur2  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.066 r2=0.044 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  leg on tibia2  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.052 r2=0.027 blend=0.014 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus2 from=0.00 to=0.72 r=0.030 r2=0.013 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus2 from=0.72 to=1.00 r=0.013 r2=0.000 blend=0.003 chamfer mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60

  bar  leg on femur3  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.066 r2=0.044 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  leg on tibia3  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.052 r2=0.027 blend=0.014 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus3 from=0.00 to=0.72 r=0.030 r2=0.013 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus3 from=0.72 to=1.00 r=0.013 r2=0.000 blend=0.003 chamfer mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60

  bar  leg on femur4  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.066 r2=0.044 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  leg on tibia4  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.052 r2=0.027 blend=0.014 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus4 from=0.00 to=0.72 r=0.030 r2=0.013 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on tarsus4 from=0.72 to=1.00 r=0.013 r2=0.000 blend=0.003 chamfer mirror color=2a1420 gloss=0.60

# Wound pass: hidden bone. Auto-derive handles the limbs; the skull is
# authored because a headshot is the shot players take.
bones
  ratio 0.38
  # Cranium bone inside the flesh cranium (semi 0.075 x 0.103 x 0.099) with
  # ~1.5 cm of meat on every side.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 r=0.075 wide=0.80 tall=1.12 deep=1.08
  # Torso bones AUTHORED, for the budget as much as the anatomy: auto-derive
  # would put a bone inside each orb and each hip mass (~9 prims). A spine
  # through the waist, a ribcage, and a cephalothorax plate the legs hang off.
  bar  torso on spine  from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.030
  blob torso on chest  at=0.45 r=0.070 wide=1.20 tall=1.10 deep=0.80
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 r=0.120 wide=1.10 tall=0.60 deep=1.30 offset=(0,0,-0.080)
  # Two more authored purely for the BUDGET (124 -> 120 of the shader's 128):
  # an authored bone replaces derivation on its whole bone (build-body.ts),
  # so one bar here stands in for the two derived from shoulder ball + upper
  # arm, and from leg2's coxa + femur.
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.02 to=0.96 r=0.015 mirror
  bar  leg on femur2   from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.021 mirror

# No mesh, so no bake: every face feature is a prim above and the face block
# is a NUB (headRadius ~0) so the parameterised ellipsoid cannot fight the
# authored cranium. Same road as ogre / bloatmaw / gnasher.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# The generated face sheet is OFF. With no sheet block the lab multiplies the
# shared default sheet over the head, and on this face it painted white
# greasepaint patches around the eyes (the default's eye glow region). Every
# feature here is a prim, so there is nothing for a sheet to add.
sheet
  enabled 0

# Skin: pale and cool — porcelain gone slightly grey, a body that lives in the
# dark — with a bruise-VIOLET mottle (a hue shift, not a darker base, or it
# vanishes). Wet and translucent: she should look soft and a little
# see-through at the rim, which is the beautiful half; the sheen on the legs
# and sac is the other half. Linear RGB; the sRGB encode lifts it.
palette
  baseColor     0.520 0.420 0.420
  deepColor     0.520 0.060 0.100
  charColor     0.070 0.055 0.060
  specIntensity 0.55
  specRoughness 0.32
  fresnelBoost  0.40
  translucency  0.30
  wetness       0.45
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.020
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.006
  mottleAmp     0.38
  mottleScale   2.0
  mottleColor   0.300 0.200 0.360
